In dev3 builds, at least, some of the python tests were failing.
This is because they pick up a pytest plugin ctest_measurements_reporter
provided by Gaudi.  This adds DartMeasurement xml entities to the log
output, which includes the source of the test.  However, the test source
contains the string ERROR, which the test runner sees and thus concludes
that the test fails.

We can disable this behavior by setting the environment variable
DISABLE_CTEST_MEASUREMENTS=1.
